**470 certified cells, 11 exceed the harm budget.**

### cross-mask minus hard-label
Cross-mask uses no retrieval labels; hard-label needs one per pool element.

| protocol | cells | mean | worst | best |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| cluster (cross-domain) | 40 | -0.0288 | -0.1169 | +0.0187 |
| random (in-domain) | 186 | -0.0436 | -0.3042 | +0.0578 |

Proposition 4 guarantees dominance only when the richer host is
conditionally correct.  Under the cross-domain protocol the richer host
has collapsed, the precondition fails, and cross-mask loses -- which is
what the theory predicts, not a counterexample to it.
